Discipline System
A full-featured school discipline & behavior management platform built with Django. It lets administrators, teachers, and class teachers log discipline incidents, track student risk scores, run approval workflows, and engage parents — all backed by AI-assisted analytics, gamification, attendance, timetabling, and a document vault.
Features
Core Discipline Management
- Discipline categories — 24 built-in offense categories (attendance, academic, uniform, bullying, fighting, theft, substance, exam, etc.) each with a configurable risk_weight (1–5) and severity_level.
- Discipline reports — log incidents against a student with a rating (Very Minor → Very Serious). Points are computed as rating_base_points × category.risk_weight.
- Risk scoring — each student has a risk_score (0–100) and risk_level (GOOD / WARNING / CRITICAL). Scores auto-recompute from reports; CRITICAL is ≥60, WARNING is 30–59.
- Explainable risk — Student.explain_risk() returns human-readable drivers, trend, and level reasoning for fair/legal defensibility.
Workflow & Governance
- Approval workflow — serious/critical reports (risk_weight ≥ 4) are auto-flagged for mandatory second sign-off (PENDING / APPROVED / REJECTED).
- Resolution & interventions — assign reports, set follow-up dates, mark resolved, and record intervention notes.
- Sanctions — link detention, community service, suspension, counseling, parent meetings, etc. to reports with lifecycle status.
- Appeals — students/parents can dispute reports; overturning soft-deletes the original report.
- Immutable audit trail — ReportHistory snapshots every mutation (create/update/approve/reject/resolve/delete/restore).
User Roles & Safety
- Roles — School Admin (superuser), Teacher, Class Teacher, Parent/Guardian.
- Teacher approval — teachers register and require admin approval before activation; suspend/ban/delete controls included.
- Rate limiting & anomaly tracking — RateLimitLog throttles per-teacher/per-student daily reports.
- Soft delete & archival — discipline records and students are never hard-deleted; they are soft-deleted/archived with reason and actor for data protection/retention.
Engagement
- Notifications — in-app critical/warning/info/success alerts to class teachers and admins.
- Parent communication log — every outbound email/SMS/push/letter is recorded with consent flagging (GDPR-style audit).
- Parent portal — parents view linked children, reports, and notifications.
AI & Analytics
- AI recommendation engine — global, per-student, and per-class recommendations, risk stats, trend analysis, predictive analysis, behavior patterns, and intervention-effectiveness endpoints.
- AI chat — conversational assistant with student-context awareness.
- Aether AI — secondary chat integration (aether_integration.py).
- Dashboards — admin, class-teacher, teacher, analytics, gamification, Aether, and mobile dashboards.
Gamification
- Student points — award/penalize points for positive behavior, interventions, perfect attendance, academic excellence, etc.
- Rewards & leaderboards — badges, certificates, prizes; weekly/monthly/termly/yearly/all-time leaderboards.
School Operations
- School setup — school profile, grade levels, academic terms, streams, subjects.
- Bulk student upload — Excel/CSV template (student_upload_template.xlsx).
- Attendance — QR/NFC/manual/biometric check-in with status tracking.
- Timetable — entries per stream/form/day with conflict checks.
- Document vault — versioned, confidential-capable document storage (report cards, certificates, IDs, etc.).
- Reporting & export — export discipline reports in multiple formats.
API
- REST API (/rest/...) — JWT-auth endpoints for students, reports, attendance, timetable, leaderboard, rewards, documents, analytics, parent views, and a health check.
- AI API (/ai/api/...) — JSON endpoints powering the recommendation engine and dashboards.
Tech Stack
- Backend: Django 5.2 (Python 3.11/3.13)
- Database: SQLite (dev) → PostgreSQL (prod, via dj-database-url / psycopg2)
- API: Django REST Framework + SimpleJWT, django-filter, django-taggit
- Realtime/Comms: Channels, SendGrid (email), qrcode
- Auth/Security: django-otp (2FA), CORS headers
- Storage: django-storages + boto3 (S3 for media in prod)
- Static/Prod: WhiteNoise, Gunicorn
- Data tooling: pandas, openpyxl, Pillow
Project Structure
-discipline-system/
├── core/                  # Main Django app (models, views, urls, api, signals, middleware)
│   ├── models.py          # All domain models
│   ├── views.py           # Web views & dashboards
│   ├── api.py             # REST API endpoints
│   ├── ai_chat.py         # AI chat logic
│   ├── aether_integration.py
│   ├── automation.py      # Scheduled/automated tasks
│   ├── notifications.py
│   ├── migrations/
│   └── management/commands/  # init_data, seed_categories, run_automation, etc.
├── disciplinary_program/ # Django project settings, wsgi
├── templates/            # HTML templates (dashboards, portals, emails)
├── static/ / staticfiles/ / media/
├── supabase/             # Supabase config (optional backend)
├── requirements.txt
├── vercel.json           # Vercel deployment config
└── manage.py
Installation
# Clone
git clone <repo-url>
cd -discipline-system
# Create & activate virtualenv
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
# Configure environment (see .env)
cp .env.example .env            # edit as needed
# Apply migrations & seed
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py init_data      # or: manage.py seed_categories
python manage.py createsuperuser
# Run
python manage.py runserver
Configuration (.env)
Key settings (loaded via python-dotenv):
- DEBUG — True/False
- SECRET_KEY
- DATABASE_URL — PostgreSQL connection string for production
- DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE — disciplinary_program.settings
- Email (SendGrid) and storage (S3) credentials for production
Key Management Commands
- python manage.py init_data — seed initial school/categories data
- python manage.py seed_categories — populate discipline categories
- python manage.py run_automation — run scheduled automation tasks
- python manage.py show_errors — surface runtime errors
- python manage.py cleanup_profiles — tidy orphaned profiles
Deployment
Configured for Vercel (vercel.json): builds the WSGI app via @vercel/python (runtime python3.11) and serves static/media files. Production uses PostgreSQL (Supabase-compatible) and S3 storage via django-storages.
vercel deploy
